# Cloudflare Pages _headers file
# ================================================================
# Put this file at the ROOT of the repo, right alongside index.html
# (same folder, NOT inside a subfolder). Cloudflare Pages picks it up
# automatically on the next deploy — no dashboard setting needed.
#
# What this fixes: without this, a phone that already has the app added
# to its home screen can keep showing an OLD cached copy of index.html /
# supabase-client.js indefinitely, even after a new version is deployed —
# which is exactly the "won't open from the home screen icon, but opens
# fine from a fresh link" symptom. These two files are small and change
# often, so they should never be cached — the browser should always ask
# Cloudflare "is there a newer version?" before using what it has.
#
# (Everything else — fonts, external CDN libraries — is unaffected and
# keeps its normal caching, only these two files are forced to
# always-revalidate.)

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

/supabase-client.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
